---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Probe EVM RPC providers: method support, archive state, latency, subscriptions, rate limits and cross-provider consistency

Usage: rustman evm probe [OPTIONS] <RPC_OR_ENV>...

Arguments:
  <RPC_OR_ENV>...
          Providers: URLs (http, https, ws, wss), {{variables}}, or names of environments whose {{rpc}} is probed

Options:
      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --methods <LIST>
          Methods to probe: standard, all, or a comma-separated list
          
          [default: standard]

      --block <N>
          Block of the archive check (default 1000000, at most head - 10000)

      --budget <N>
          Requests per provider at most
          
          [default: 500]

      --report <FORMAT[=PATH]>
          Render the report as json, junit, markdown, html or sarif, written to a file or stdout, as in html=probe.html (repeatable)

      --viz
          Show the results in the graphical viz companion (rustman-viz)

      --rate-discovery
          Search for each provider's rate limit with eth_blockNumber at 5, 10, 20 and 40 req/s

      --max-rate <N>
          Highest rate tried by --rate-discovery, in req/s
          
          [default: 40]

      --max-drift <BLOCKS>
          Head drift (in blocks) above which a provider is a medium finding
          
          [default: 3]

      --drift-interval <DURATION>
          Time between the 5 head samples of the drift check (default 2.5s: 10 s in all)

      --call <ADDRESS:CALLDATA>
          An eth_call compared across providers and traced: <address>:<calldata>

      --address <ADDRESS>
          Address of the balance and state checks (default: the zero address)

      --fail-on <SEVERITY>
          Exit 1 when a finding is at or above this severity: critical, high, medium, low or info
          
          [default: high]

      --rate <N>
          Requests per second per provider (default: [safety].rate, 10)

      --concurrency <N>
          Requests in flight per provider (default: [safety].concurrency, 4)

      --production <HOST>
          Confirm a production host (repeatable)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per node call: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman evm probe https://rpc-a.example https://rpc-b.example
  rustman evm probe mainnet-alchemy mainnet-infura --methods all --report html=probe.html
  rustman evm probe wss://rpc-a.example --rate-discovery --max-rate 20
  rustman evm probe https://rpc-a.example --call 0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48:0x18160ddd --viz
